Yes. For Sepo + ACPX, configure **bare model IDs** in `model`, and configure reasoning separately in `reasoning_effort`.

Do **not** use `gpt-5.5/medium` as the Sepo model config unless you are intentionally relying on a Codex/ACPX shorthand. Sepo’s cleaner config should be:

```json
{ "model": "gpt-5.5", "reasoning_effort": "medium" }
```

ACPX supports `--model <id>` and notes that model support depends on the underlying agent/adapter: https://github.com/openclaw/acpx/blob/main/docs/CLI.md#global-options

Recommended `AGENT_MODEL_POLICY` shape:

```json
{
  "providers": {
    "codex": {
      "model": "gpt-5.5",
      "reasoning_effort": "high"
    },
    "claude": {
      "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
      "reasoning_effort": "high"
    }
  },
  "route_overrides": {
    "answer": {
      "provider": "codex",
      "model": "gpt-5.4-mini",
      "reasoning_effort": "medium"
    },
    "implement": {
      "provider": "codex",
      "model": "gpt-5.5",
      "reasoning_effort": "high"
    },
    "fix-pr": {
      "provider": "codex",
      "model": "gpt-5.5",
      "reasoning_effort": "high"
    },
    "review-synthesize": {
      "provider": "codex",
      "model": "gpt-5.5",
      "reasoning_effort": "high"
    }
  }
}
```

Current useful model IDs:

| Provider | Good default | Stronger / coding-heavy | Cheaper |
|---|---|---|---|
| Codex/OpenAI | `gpt-5.5` | `gpt-5.3-codex` or `gpt-5.5` | `gpt-5.4-mini` |
| Claude Code | `claude-sonnet-4-6` | `claude-opus-4-8` | `claude-haiku-4-5` |

OpenAI docs list `gpt-5.5` as the current frontier model and show reasoning efforts `none`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`: https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-5.5/

OpenAI also lists `gpt-5.3-codex` as the current agentic coding model with `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`: https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-5.3-codex/

Claude docs list Claude Code aliases and current resolutions: `sonnet` -> Sonnet 4.6, `opus` -> Opus 4.8 on Anthropic API, and `haiku` -> Haiku 4.5: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/model-config

Important caveat: Claude Code aliases like `sonnet`, `opus`, and `haiku` are convenient but move over time. If we want stable Sepo behavior, use full/pinned IDs like `claude-sonnet-4-6` or `claude-opus-4-8`.

